ecade":-0.237,"lo":-0.51,"hi":0.036,"class":"edge","n":100,"first":1915,"last":2025,"intercept":49.54072516620075,"slope":-0.023675773651175434,"total":-2.6},"snow_normal":1.4},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Muscle Shoals has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Muscle Shoals' nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1983.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 52\u00b0F was the 21st coolest November 13 high (tied) of 132 since 1893, the coolest since 2022.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 84% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>52\u00b0F</strong> was the 21st coolest November 13 high (tied) of 132 since 1893, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 64\u00b0F, and the record is 80\u00b0F (1909, 1916). The low of <strong>36\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Muscle Shoals has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Muscle Shoals' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Muscle Shoals has set <strong class=\"sig\">18 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 75 that chance alone would give, and <strong>97 record highs</strong>, more than the 75 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (57). Muscle Shoals' all-time high is 108\u00b0F, on June 26, 1914.","t_chg":"Muscle Shoals' nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1983.","p_chg":"Across 121 complete years: Muscle Shoals' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.24), about +2.3\u00b0F since 1893. Muscle Shoals' average high shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.15) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1983, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.64\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.35 to +0.93) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.83\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.49 to +1.18). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 10 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Muscle Shoals' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.37 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 53.6 inches a year. The wettest year was 1975 (78.78 in); the driest, 1943 (30.92 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}